      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think unhiding these constants is the right solution. AFAICT the app-facing API that actually reports these errors is:\n\n    method public void onError(@NonNull android.net.QosCallbackException);\n\nand it passes exceptions, not integers. It seems like a mistake to unhide the integer. Instead, what we should do is switch to the exception everywhere: deprecate the int version of sendQosCallbackError and in its place use a version that takes an int and a QosCallbackException.\n\nSewook, would that work?",
      "revId": "d590adace8d1d23c53eb6ae2f17be96a5a725501",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
